WEBVTT

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:44.090
Which one should I make?

00:01:44.090 --> 00:01:46.210
Who are you giving it to?

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:47.960
I'm going to eat them with my friends.

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:50.560
Just as I thought. I knew it was like that.

00:01:51.350 --> 00:01:55.070
Exchanging chocolate between girls is really fun, you know.

00:01:55.690 --> 00:01:59.820
Aztec culture. Toffee. Cocoa.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:08.250
Haruka-neesama.

00:02:08.780 --> 00:02:10.420
What is it, Chiaki?

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:12.790
Please teach me how to make some too.

00:02:13.750 --> 00:02:16.500
Oh, sure. How about you, Kana?

00:02:16.840 --> 00:02:22.050
Nah... count me out. I don't want to have anything to do with Valentine's Day.

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:28.600
I assume with your impudent nature, you're just going to swipe chocolates from the popular guys.

00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:32.280
What? What's wrong?

00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:37.440
I see! I can eat all I want!

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:41.740
Hey... I'm not giving you any nice suggestions here.

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:45.570
It's a rare occasion, so let's make them together, Kana.

00:02:45.570 --> 00:02:48.750
Eh? I'm fine.

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:52.610
Besides, it's better receiving than giving anyway.

00:02:52.610 --> 00:02:56.020
That won't do. This is a festival for girls.

00:02:56.020 --> 00:02:56.820
Right, Chiaki?

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:58.930
Eh? Yeah...

00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:01.340
So let's make them together, okay?

00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:05.850
A celebration? Festival... Festival.

00:03:06.350 --> 00:03:11.890
This is revenge. Haruka's hospitality on Pajama's Festival was seamless.

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:15.440
Are you trying to do something pointless again?

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:18.770
All right! Let's gather everyone.

00:03:18.770 --> 00:03:20.070
Valentine's Festival!

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:22.740
Hey...

00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:35.230
Is everyone ready?!

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:36.500
Yes!

00:03:39.090 --> 00:03:41.760
Why do I have to dress like this?

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:43.610
What are you saying?

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:46.350
You're Mako-chan. You're a girl.

00:03:46.350 --> 00:03:48.570
Valentine's Day is a festival for girls.

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:50.680
There's no way you can refuse to participate.

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:52.840
Yeah, but I...

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:54.820
Are you trying to say you're not a girl?

00:03:55.570 --> 00:03:57.520
Looks like our friendship was short-lived.

00:03:59.240 --> 00:04:00.300
Huh?

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:03.240
H-Hey! Wait a minute!

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:03.780
What?

00:04:04.160 --> 00:04:08.780
You mean... I'm not allowed to come here anymore?

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:19.290
No, I'll do it! I'll do my best to help out!

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:29.870
Haruka-san, what should I do?

00:04:29.870 --> 00:04:31.930
What kind of chocolate do you want to make?

00:04:32.380 --> 00:04:35.780
Hmm, something that's cute!

00:04:35.780 --> 00:04:37.900
Okay. Then...

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:40.320
First, break up the chocolate.

00:04:41.130 --> 00:04:43.570
Then break them up into even smaller pieces.

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:45.250
Okay!

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:51.210
Hey! What am I here for?

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:53.450
Because it's a festival.

00:04:53.450 --> 00:04:55.040
Oh...

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:57.660
Do you plan on giving them out?

00:04:57.660 --> 00:04:58.640
Chocolate?

00:04:58.640 --> 00:05:00.740
I don't give out those things.

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:02.460
What about your brothers?

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:06.200
Give them to my brothers? No way.

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:08.980
Is that so? What a lonely person.

00:05:08.980 --> 00:05:11.910
I'm lonely?

00:05:14.390 --> 00:05:16.620
Oh, she's here.

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:19.880
I've been waiting for you! Come on in!

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:22.410
Sorry to disturb.

00:05:22.410 --> 00:05:24.070
Oh, welcome!

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:26.110
It sure is lively.

00:05:31.170 --> 00:05:34.590
Am I... lonely?

00:05:38.640 --> 00:05:40.000
Is it going well?

00:05:40.370 --> 00:05:43.230
Yeah... kind of.

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:45.210
Who are you going to give it to, Chiaki?

00:05:47.110 --> 00:05:49.180
Who are you going to give your chocolate to, Uchida?

00:05:49.540 --> 00:05:52.710
Ah, I haven't thought about it.

00:05:52.710 --> 00:05:54.850
What an imprudent person.

00:05:58.490 --> 00:06:03.140
Yoshino! Who are you giving your chocolate to?

00:06:03.140 --> 00:06:06.360
I'm giving them to my dad. I made it yesterday.

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:09.010
What the? How dull.

00:06:09.010 --> 00:06:11.450
So who are you giving it to, Kana-chan?

00:06:12.320 --> 00:06:13.720
I'll only be receiving.

00:06:20.600 --> 00:06:24.290
Sorry to ask both of you to help me out.

00:06:25.010 --> 00:06:26.240
I don't mind.

00:06:26.920 --> 00:06:29.480
That's right. We have nothing to do anyway.

00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:31.550
Thank you.

00:06:31.550 --> 00:06:33.730
You're getting in the way! Get out!

00:06:33.730 --> 00:06:35.060
Why?!

00:06:35.060 --> 00:06:36.910
You're SO stingy!

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:39.790
Kana-chan is energetic as usual.

00:06:39.790 --> 00:06:40.940
You're right...

00:06:41.530 --> 00:06:44.150
Who are you giving your chocolate to, Mako-chan?

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:49.390
Haruka-san.

00:06:49.390 --> 00:06:50.740
Take that back!

00:06:51.020 --> 00:06:52.610
Uh... well...

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:54.160
I said take that back!

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:57.170
Geez, Chiaki...

00:06:57.170 --> 00:06:58.280
Thank you.

00:06:58.280 --> 00:07:01.670
But since it's a rare occasion, how about giving it to a boy?

00:07:01.670 --> 00:07:02.540
Eh?

00:07:02.950 --> 00:07:04.480
Is there someone you can give it to?

00:07:06.390 --> 00:07:07.880
Do you have anyone in mind?

00:07:07.880 --> 00:07:10.460
Oh? So there's such a person?

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:13.640
Well...

00:07:15.990 --> 00:07:18.350
M–Makoto-kun...

00:07:20.910 --> 00:07:23.600
Eh?! So you know Makoto-kun?

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:26.860
Uh, yeah... you can say that.

00:07:27.480 --> 00:07:29.540
I won't say anything bad.

00:07:29.540 --> 00:07:32.880
Give up on him. He's a dumb kid.

00:07:32.880 --> 00:07:34.360
N–No way...

00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:40.220
Chocolate really tastes great.

00:07:40.220 --> 00:07:42.850
Is this okay? This chocolate was meant to be used.

00:07:42.850 --> 00:07:45.330
It's fine. It's fine.

00:07:48.490 --> 00:07:49.630
Say...

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:52.790
Am I really a lonely person?

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:55.800
What? Is that a philosophical question?

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:13.500
Are you okay there?

00:08:13.500 --> 00:08:15.320
I'm fine.

00:08:22.950 --> 00:08:24.710
Wow!

00:08:24.710 --> 00:08:26.620
Yeah, it turned out quite well.

00:08:26.620 --> 00:08:29.260
I was so nervous and I wasn't even the one making it.

00:08:29.260 --> 00:08:31.670
Silly. We've barely started.

00:08:37.090 --> 00:08:38.500
Where are you going?

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:39.590
Bathroom.

00:08:42.020 --> 00:08:46.240
Eh? It's not melting properly.

00:08:56.910 --> 00:09:00.490
Low flame. Very low flame.

00:09:00.490 --> 00:09:04.400
Not bad. Melted chocolate tastes pretty good too.

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:05.870
Hey! What are you doing?

00:09:15.150 --> 00:09:17.450
Kana, you...

00:09:17.980 --> 00:09:19.930
I was sampling it and accidentally finished.

00:09:19.930 --> 00:09:22.060
<i>Get Out!</i>

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:28.710
Yup, you're doing well. Just keep stirring like that.

00:09:30.060 --> 00:09:32.220
You're doing great, Mako-chan.

00:09:32.220 --> 00:09:34.520
At this rate, you can be a bride anytime.

00:09:37.580 --> 00:09:38.640
B–Bride...

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:40.660
Hey, I smell something burnt.

00:09:41.090 --> 00:09:43.890
Oh no, what should I do?!

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:45.700
All right, I'm coming!

00:09:48.480 --> 00:09:50.140
Mako-chan?

00:09:55.310 --> 00:09:59.010
Touma. Touma! Get up!

00:10:00.060 --> 00:10:02.040
What is it?

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:03.390
It seems we don't have enough chocolate.

00:10:03.980 --> 00:10:05.130
That's because...

00:10:05.130 --> 00:10:07.650
Go buy some. Right now!

00:10:07.650 --> 00:10:08.630
Me?!

00:10:08.630 --> 00:10:09.610
Didn't you eat the chocolate?

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:11.380
Huh?

00:10:11.530 --> 00:10:14.550
Go and buy some right now, you idiot!

00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:16.150
All right.

00:10:22.140 --> 00:10:23.280
What the heck?

00:10:23.950 --> 00:10:25.520
Seriously...

00:10:26.810 --> 00:10:28.900
Didn't Kana also eat the chocolate?

00:10:28.900 --> 00:10:30.900
Hey, Touma!

00:10:31.220 --> 00:10:32.870
Oh, Fujioka.

00:10:33.450 --> 00:10:35.830
What's up? Are you returning from shopping?

00:10:35.830 --> 00:10:39.420
Yeah, Kana asked me to buy chocolate.

00:10:40.380 --> 00:10:41.830
Minami? Why?

00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:46.770
Well, because I was asked to help make chocolate.

00:10:47.330 --> 00:10:51.420
Do you need a hand from a guy? If so, I'll come with you.

00:10:51.530 --> 00:10:52.700
You can't!

00:10:52.700 --> 00:10:53.370
Why?

00:10:53.370 --> 00:10:58.340
Well, you see... it might be made for you.

00:10:58.340 --> 00:11:00.160
It's very likely she doesn't want you to see it.

00:11:03.780 --> 00:11:05.870
L–Later!

00:11:09.990 --> 00:11:11.940
Minami's... chocolate...

00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:17.590
I've bought it!

00:11:18.430 --> 00:11:20.410
You're slow, Touma.

00:11:20.410 --> 00:11:23.500
I ran into an awkward situation because of you.

00:11:23.500 --> 00:11:24.050
Huh?

00:11:26.070 --> 00:11:29.280
After it hardens, you can start putting on the decorations.

00:11:41.540 --> 00:11:43.490
Is it hardened yet?

00:11:43.490 --> 00:11:44.070
Not yet. Not yet.

00:11:45.490 --> 00:11:47.620
Like I said, not yet.

00:11:48.230 --> 00:11:50.510
Looks like that's that.

00:11:50.510 --> 00:11:51.750
Let's go have some tea.

00:11:51.750 --> 00:11:53.430
Yay!

00:12:06.590 --> 00:12:07.980
Where's Touma?

00:12:08.720 --> 00:12:11.460
She went home after shopping.

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:13.380
She said she was tired.

00:12:13.380 --> 00:12:15.520
She didn't do a single thing.

00:12:15.990 --> 00:12:18.550
Mako-chan left too.

00:12:18.550 --> 00:12:20.470
What an impatient person.

00:12:20.470 --> 00:12:24.280
I received Mako-chan's chocolate. I guess I'm lucky.

00:12:24.280 --> 00:12:28.470
But I wonder if it's ok for her, not giving it to Makoto-kun.

00:12:28.960 --> 00:12:30.320
It's good.

00:12:30.460 --> 00:12:33.040
I suppose she's realized that he's an idiot.

00:12:37.210 --> 00:12:39.640
Haruka, give me some chocolate.

00:12:39.640 --> 00:12:42.460
Sure. Feel free to eat the leftovers.

00:12:46.620 --> 00:12:48.980
Let's have a second cup!

00:12:48.980 --> 00:12:52.010
My my. Sorry, are you okay there?

00:12:52.010 --> 00:12:53.190
Yup!

00:12:53.550 --> 00:12:56.000
By the way, who're you giving your chocolate to, Chiaki?

00:13:02.920 --> 00:13:05.700
Ah, it's got to be him.

00:13:05.700 --> 00:13:07.470
Our neighbor, Fuyuki.

00:13:07.470 --> 00:13:08.220
Huh?

00:13:08.220 --> 00:13:09.020
Ah!

00:13:09.020 --> 00:13:11.200
Eh? So that's it.

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:13.160
I never noticed.

00:13:13.440 --> 00:13:14.410
You're wrong!

00:13:14.410 --> 00:13:16.030
No need to be shy.

00:13:16.480 --> 00:13:19.590
What kind of nonsense are you spouting?

00:13:19.590 --> 00:13:23.210
Now now, it doesn't matter who it's for,
as long as they're happy.

00:13:23.680 --> 00:13:27.090
My, it's great to be young.

00:13:45.890 --> 00:13:46.530
Yum.

00:13:50.440 --> 00:13:55.660
How is it? Taste good?
That chocolate was specifically made for you.

00:13:55.660 --> 00:14:00.260
You're shedding tears even. I didn't think you'd be so happy.

00:14:12.850 --> 00:14:15.330
It's not turning out well for me.

00:14:15.330 --> 00:14:17.130
Chiaki, help me.

00:14:17.130 --> 00:14:20.120
Be quiet. Don't talk to me right now.

00:14:20.640 --> 00:14:22.640
But...

00:14:22.640 --> 00:14:24.730
Here, I'll help you.

00:14:32.670 --> 00:14:36.100
Um... Haruka-neesama. I'm sorry.

00:14:36.100 --> 00:14:37.810
But if you look at me like that...

00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:39.960
Sorry, Chiaki. Please continue what you're doing.

00:14:40.560 --> 00:14:42.460
All done!

00:14:42.850 --> 00:14:44.680
It's nicely done.

00:14:44.680 --> 00:14:45.960
Looks delicious.

00:14:46.560 --> 00:14:48.170
It's finished.

00:14:48.170 --> 00:14:51.680
It would be great if there was a boy for me to give it to.

00:14:51.680 --> 00:14:55.420
Only an elementary student and you're already interested in the opposite sex.

00:14:55.420 --> 00:14:58.350
Someone who only eats chocolate without doing anything has no right to say that.

00:14:58.780 --> 00:15:02.730
As long as a person gets the love, the chocolate becomes a leftover.

00:15:02.730 --> 00:15:05.900
And there are others who are content with just the leftovers.

00:15:06.620 --> 00:15:09.860
Valentine's Day really is terrific.

00:15:16.060 --> 00:15:17.690
Morning, Fujioka!

00:15:17.690 --> 00:15:19.180
Oh, morning!

00:15:26.900 --> 00:15:28.370
Oh no!

00:15:28.370 --> 00:15:30.720
I can't accept even one obligatory chocolate today.

00:15:32.400 --> 00:15:34.510
I have to return them.

00:15:34.590 --> 00:15:36.960
But, who gave me these...?

00:15:36.960 --> 00:15:38.560
Fujioka!

00:15:41.100 --> 00:15:42.350
Good morning, Minami!

00:15:42.800 --> 00:15:45.330
Did you receive a lot of chocolate, Fujioka?!

00:15:45.650 --> 00:15:47.690
Not a single one!

00:15:47.690 --> 00:15:49.050
Eh?

00:15:52.180 --> 00:15:55.390
I-I see...

00:15:56.200 --> 00:15:59.870
I have to find a chance to give this chocolate to Fujioka-kun.

00:15:59.870 --> 00:16:01.870
It would be great if he accepts it.

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:07.960
What's this?

00:16:07.960 --> 00:16:11.010
Is she preventing people from giving Fujioka-kun chocolate?

00:16:15.020 --> 00:16:17.010
What a nuisance.

00:16:19.110 --> 00:16:21.020
Move away already.

00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:25.020
How long does she plan to stand there?

00:16:26.060 --> 00:16:28.740
It really doesn't seem like he's receiving any chocolate.

00:16:32.800 --> 00:16:35.360
Hamu-chan, here!

00:16:35.930 --> 00:16:37.570
Looks tasty, doesn't it?

00:16:40.810 --> 00:16:43.380
Does Hamu-chan want chocolate too?

00:16:47.220 --> 00:16:50.110
My chocolate!

00:16:50.110 --> 00:16:51.920
Don't go feeding it as you please.

00:16:57.940 --> 00:16:59.950
Touma, please accept my chocolate.

00:17:00.070 --> 00:17:00.920
Me?

00:17:00.920 --> 00:17:04.400
Yup. Because Touma is way cooler than the boys.

00:17:04.400 --> 00:17:05.730
I don't need any.

00:17:05.730 --> 00:17:08.060
Hey, give us some too.

00:17:08.620 --> 00:17:10.190
Here, take this.

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:13.070
Huh?

00:17:14.520 --> 00:17:17.700
From now on, you're a genuine guy.

00:17:29.080 --> 00:17:31.820
Haruka! Let me try some of your chocolate.

00:17:32.230 --> 00:17:36.630
As I thought, anything Haruka makes is delicious.

00:17:41.990 --> 00:17:45.200
What're you doing, Hosaka-senpai?

00:17:46.090 --> 00:17:50.310
I was wondering when the best time to give this to her was.

00:17:50.310 --> 00:17:51.440
What's that?

00:17:56.390 --> 00:17:59.450
This was made using Belgian chocolate of the finest grade.

00:17:59.450 --> 00:18:02.680
This is the cake that I've made with all the skills I possess.

00:18:03.170 --> 00:18:05.440
Then... what's it for?

00:18:05.440 --> 00:18:08.960
A return gift for Minami Haruka on White Day of course.

00:18:09.640 --> 00:18:11.240
Return gift?

00:18:11.240 --> 00:18:15.170
I don't recall Haruka giving you any chocolate.

00:18:15.170 --> 00:18:22.140
That's true, but Valentine's Day is only for today. I'll have to act with a plan in mind...

00:18:28.530 --> 00:18:29.820
Okay!

00:18:32.090 --> 00:18:33.230
Keiko.

00:18:34.350 --> 00:18:36.970
Who's the most popular guy in our school?

00:18:36.970 --> 00:18:38.010
Huh?

00:18:40.120 --> 00:18:42.400
Ishikawa-senpai I think.

00:18:42.400 --> 00:18:43.530
I see.

00:18:43.530 --> 00:18:44.600
Probably.

00:18:45.050 --> 00:18:48.000
Good! He must have a lot of extras.

00:18:51.160 --> 00:18:52.650
But why–

00:18:52.650 --> 00:18:54.000
She's gone...

00:18:54.830 --> 00:18:56.030
Now's the time!

00:19:02.780 --> 00:19:03.890
Eh?

00:19:05.480 --> 00:19:08.080
Do you know where Fujioka-kun went?

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:11.290
He was busy going around returning chocolate.

00:19:11.810 --> 00:19:13.560
Maybe he dislikes chocolate?

00:19:14.100 --> 00:19:16.880
No way...

00:19:22.270 --> 00:19:25.320
I've brought the printouts for the next class.

00:19:25.320 --> 00:19:28.670
Huh? You brought them even though we aren't from the same class. Thank you.

00:19:28.670 --> 00:19:30.660
It's nothing. It was just on the way.

00:19:30.660 --> 00:19:33.070
Thank you. Here's chocolate for you.

00:19:33.070 --> 00:19:35.230
I'm fine, really.

00:19:35.230 --> 00:19:36.740
Here's some from me too.

00:19:37.290 --> 00:19:39.220
Just accept it. Here!

00:19:39.220 --> 00:19:42.820
Okay. Thank you for your generosity.

00:19:42.820 --> 00:19:45.450
Aren't you going to give him chocolate, Chiaki?

00:19:45.450 --> 00:19:46.430
Why should I?

00:19:46.430 --> 00:19:47.690
It's not for him?

00:19:47.690 --> 00:19:48.810
That goes without saying.

00:19:58.820 --> 00:20:02.490
All of them have been returned.

00:20:02.490 --> 00:20:05.750
But in the end, I still haven't received anything from Minami.

00:20:06.970 --> 00:20:08.640
Fujioka!

00:20:16.500 --> 00:20:20.750
What the? Judging from your expression, you didn't receive any.

00:20:21.440 --> 00:20:25.370
I have a lot here. I'll share some with the unpopular you.

00:20:27.140 --> 00:20:28.260
Okay.

00:20:30.050 --> 00:20:31.470
Thank you!

00:20:39.550 --> 00:20:42.480
Here, my Valentine's gifts for both of you.

00:20:43.900 --> 00:20:44.950
All right!

00:20:46.570 --> 00:20:49.410
Thank you very much, Haruka-neesama!

00:20:51.160 --> 00:20:54.380
So in the end, who did you give your chocolate to, Chiaki?

00:20:59.310 --> 00:21:00.630
Please accept it.

00:21:01.340 --> 00:21:02.690
For me?

00:21:09.670 --> 00:21:12.100
Thank you, Chiaki!

00:21:12.470 --> 00:21:16.640
But it would be nice if one day, you could give this to someone special besides me.

00:21:17.150 --> 00:21:20.610
My feelings for Haruka-neesama are unwavering.

00:21:21.010 --> 00:21:23.280
Hey, where's mine?

00:21:37.410 --> 00:21:40.110
It's such a waste to eat it.

00:21:40.110 --> 00:21:40.830
Really?

00:21:42.150 --> 00:21:44.050
Then I'll help myself.

00:21:47.390 --> 00:21:49.090
What the heck are you doing?!

00:21:54.420 --> 00:21:56.540
I'm tired of these black and sweet things.

00:21:56.540 --> 00:21:59.220
Go lick some salt then!

00:21:59.220 --> 00:22:01.060
Stop it! Don't!

00:23:31.610 --> 00:23:34.820
Do you know the difference between zaru soba and mori soba?

00:23:34.820 --> 00:23:37.340
In the past, different soba used different dipping sauces.

00:23:37.350 --> 00:23:38.530
Zaru soba uses first soup stock.

00:23:38.530 --> 00:23:40.270
Mori soba uses second soup stock.

00:23:40.540 --> 00:23:43.740
Right now, there's no way to tell the difference other than the dried seaweed on top of zaru soba.

00:23:43.740 --> 00:23:46.050
Ah, I want to eat soba right now!
